[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: KM271-WiFi System Architecture
UID: KM271-SYA
VERSION: 0.1
OPTIONS:
  VIEW_STYLE: Table

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: architecture.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document decomposes the KM271-WiFi into subsystems, describes the
external and internal interfaces and records the main architecture
decisions. Each element traces to the system requirements it implements
(KM271-SYS-xxx). Hardware and software requirements trace back to these
elements.

Context: the module sits in the KM271 slot of a Buderus Logamatic 2107.
It talks to the Logamatic over a 5 V asynchronous serial line (KM271
protocol, 3964R), is powered from the slot and connects to the home
network by WiFi or, with the extension, by Ethernet. A home automation
server (e.g. Home Assistant, MQTT broker) consumes the data.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: System context

[BLOCK]
UID: KM271-SYA-001
STATUS: Draft
KIND: System
TITLE: KM271-WiFi module
DESCRIPTION: >>>
Plug-in module that replaces the Buderus KM271. It bridges the KM271 service
interface of the Logamatic to IP networks and adds local sensor inputs and an
extension interface.
<<<
REALIZATION: KM217-WiFi/KM217-WiFi.kicad_sch, KM217-WiFi/KM217-WiFi.kicad_pcb
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-001

[BLOCK]
UID: KM271-SYA-002
STATUS: Draft
KIND: External
TITLE: Buderus Logamatic controller
DESCRIPTION: >>>
Heating controller with KM271 slot (2x6 card edge). Provides 5 V, GND, the
serial KM271 interface and the exhaust gas sensor circuit.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Slot supply comes from the NM 282 power board (LM317). Its source resistance
and current budget are not documented by Buderus.
<<<

[BLOCK]
UID: KM271-SYA-003
STATUS: Draft
KIND: External
TITLE: Home network and automation server
DESCRIPTION: >>>
WiFi access point or Ethernet switch, MQTT broker and/or Home Assistant
instance that receive values and send commands.
<<<

[BLOCK]
UID: KM271-SYA-004
STATUS: Draft
KIND: External
TITLE: Service PC
DESCRIPTION: >>>
PC or smartphone used for flashing (USB, browser based WebTools or esptool)
and for first-time configuration.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

