[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Architecture decisions

[DECISION]
UID: KM271-SYA-200
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: ESP32-S3 instead of ESP32
CONTEXT: >>>
The ESP32-WROOM-32D of v1.x is end of life for new designs and has no native
USB. A USB-UART bridge was needed for flashing.
<<<
DECISION: >>>
Use the ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N8R2 (8 MB flash, 2 MB quad PSRAM). Modules with
octal PSRAM are excluded because they occupy GPIO35-37.
<<<
CONSEQUENCES: >>>
All GPIO assignments changed. Firmware needs an ESP32-S3 build, an S3 specific
OTA image and a board preset.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-007
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-030

[DECISION]
UID: KM271-SYA-201
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Step-down converter instead of LDO
CONTEXT: >>>
The slot supply is weak. A linear regulator draws the full 3.3 V load current
from the slot and drops out at about 1.8 Ohm source resistance.
<<<
DECISION: >>>
Generate 3.3 V with a TPS62162 step-down converter. Keep the AZ1117 LDO
footprint as not-fitted alternative, selected by 0 Ohm resistors.
<<<
CONSEQUENCES: >>>
Lower slot current (292 mA instead of 365 mA at 360 mA load) and regulation up
to about 3 Ohm. Switching node needs careful layout (EMC).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-011
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-012

[DECISION]
UID: KM271-SYA-202
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Diode OR instead of power select jumpers
CONTEXT: >>>
v1.x used the power select header J3. Wrong jumper settings caused support
requests.
<<<
DECISION: >>>
Combine USB VBUS and the slot 5 V with Schottky diodes (D8, D9). Remove J3.
<<<
CONSEQUENCES: >>>
+5V is 0.3-0.4 V below the source. The 5 V monitor measures behind the diodes.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-013

[DECISION]
UID: KM271-SYA-203
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: USB data path selected by solder jumpers
CONTEXT: >>>
Native USB of the ESP32-S3 is sufficient for flashing and logging, but can be
disabled by faulty firmware. The CP2102N adds cost.
<<<
DECISION: >>>
Route D+/D- through the ESD protection to the three-pad solder jumpers
JP1/JP2. Default (1-2 bridged) is the ESP32-S3 native USB; re-bridging to 2-3
selects the CP2102N. The CP2102N branch may stay unpopulated.
<<<
CONSEQUENCES: Both jumpers must always be set to the same side.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-030
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-031

[DECISION]
UID: KM271-SYA-204
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: I2C without level shifter
CONTEXT: >>>
The PCA9306 level shifter of v1.x separated the external I2C. It gated the
W5500 reset line and caused confusion about pull-ups.
<<<
DECISION: >>>
Remove the PCA9306 (U6) and connect SDA/SCL directly to J7 at 3.3 V level with
one pull-up per line on the main board (R4, R30).
<<<
CONSEQUENCES: Extensions must use 3.3 V I2C levels. I2C_EXT_EN (GPIO2) is free.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-022

[DECISION]
UID: KM271-SYA-205
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: Through-hole parts as buyer options
CONTEXT: >>>
Terminals and headers are only needed by some users and raise assembly cost.
<<<
DECISION: >>>
Do not assemble J4, J5, J6 and J8 by default. The user fits them or they are
supplied loose.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-050

[[/SECTION]]
